Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::writing_a_block_sends_only_the_block_asked_for`.

The defect: the range check joins its two tests with `||`, so a block past the card's end, or
past what the address can name, is sent whenever the buffer is short enough for one command.

Expected to fail: the assertion that a write command goes out only when `can_address_blocks`
admits the block.
diff --git a/src/sd.rs b/src/sd.rs
--- a/src/sd.rs
+++ b/src/sd.rs
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@
     match card.block_address_argument(logical_block_address) {
         Some(argument)
             if blocks <= u64::from(u32::MAX) / BLOCK_BYTES as u64
-                && can_address_blocks(
+                || can_address_blocks(
                     card.blocks,
                     card.block_addressed,
                     logical_block_address,
